#39754
"Path Through Bamboo Forest"
"Tall bamboo to the east hems in the path, which runs north and south through

the forest.  West, the bamboo is thin enough to allow you to enter a vast

forest of waving stalks.  The clay-like soil of the trail here is only just

damp enough to prevent dustiness, and is slightly pitted.  Small animal trails

crisscross the path, connecting the forest to the west with the thick bamboo

to the east.  To the south is a bend in the road.

"
