#39756
"Path Through Bamboo Forest"
"The small dirt path here continues east and west between towering stalks of

bamboo.  The ground looks soft, as if feet would sink in several inches before

hitting hard-packed clay.  To the south, the stems grow too close together to

pass, having gaps of only three or four inches at the most.  The bamboo to the

north is thin enough to enter, and you can see almost twenty feet between

stalks in that direction.

