#39757
"Path Through Bamboo Forest"
"Thick green and brown stalks line the small dirt road, which makes its way

east and west through a vast forest of bamboo.  To the south, the thick stems

grow too close together to squeeze past, forming a solid wall save for the

dark openings of wildlife trails.  North, the bamboo is thin enough to

traverse easily, and the forest floor is striped by the shadows of evenly-

spaced stems.

"
