#39758
"Path Through Bamboo Forest"
"To the south, a giant bamboo stalk perhaps four feet wide towers above the

road, growing tightly with smaller ones to block exit in that direction.  The

small dirt path continues east and west through the vast bamboo forest, its

hard-packed clay looking firm to the touch.  To the north, the bamboo is thin

enough to enter, and you can see a ways into the forest.  The canopy above is

very sparse on the northern edge of the trail, but provides complete coverage

on the southern edge.

"
