"Path Through Bamboo Forest"
"This hard-packed clay trail can still be easily made out, cutting east and

west through a vast bamboo forest.  To the south, a rock wall juts up from

among thick bamboo stems.  The rock wall is covered with moss and lichen, and

very little stone shows.  North, the bamboo is thin enough to enter.  To the

east, a giant bamboo stalk can be seen towering over the south side of the

road.

