"Path Through Bamboo Forest"
"The dirt trail continues here, running east to west through the forest of

bamboo.  Overhanging stalks shade the road from sun and rain, their wide

leaves sprouting from smooth stems.  To the south, the bamboo is too thick to

pass, while to the north it thins enough to be passable.  Small ruts line the

road where runoff has streamed down it towards an unknown goal, away from some

unseen water source.

