"Path Through Bamboo Forest"
"To the south, strong green shoots grow so close together as to be impassable,

blocking both vision and movement.  The slightly blackened bamboo to the north

is older, and seems full of decay.  An unhealthy odor wafts towards you from

that direction.  To the east, the road continues into a forest which is more

open, and can be entered to the north.  To the west, it looks like the trail

once continued on through the bamboo, but it has since become overgrown.

Perhaps the road will someday be reopened.

