tangled masses of blackened stalks above.  Fungus grows about the base of each

shoot, and a musty smell hangs in the air.  Small and large bones alike are

scattered about the ground, scored by many teeth.  West, the trail leads into

utter darkness, where strange noises can be heard.  East leads out into a

lighter, more wholesome section of the trail.

