and west.  The water is crystal clear and harbors incredible forms of life;

enormous water bugs and crustaceans can be seen in the depths.  These are

dwarfed however, by the redwood-sized bamboo and tree-sized grass that grow in

profusion around the spring, forming a seemingly impenetrable wall of green.

An aura of benevolence in the air is almost tangible, seeming to swaddle the

spring protectively.

