#39851
"Atop an Ancient Guard Tower"
"A spectacular view of the surrounding land spreads out in all directions,

painted in the gentle green, brown, and grey pastels of bamboo and swamplands.

Ancient stones held together by crumbling mortar form a battlement wall around

the top of this small tower.  The roof of the tower is about fifteen by

fifteen feet, and nearly perfectly square.  At each corner of the battlement

are rusting iron poles, which once may have held flags.  A small trapdoor was

once in the center of the floor, but it has long rotted away, leaving a

rectangular hole where a small ladder leads down into the tower.  A small,

decrepit iron ladder leader over the outside edge of the tower.

