gets gradually taller, eventually reaching impossible heights.

"
E
"east"
"The bamboo below continues for a short way, but then gives way to the more

sparse shrubbery of the swamplands.  The walls of Sos-kul are barely visible

through the ever-present swamp mist.

"
E
"west"
"Just to the northwest, the green-brown bamboo fades, becoming more brown, then

grey, and finally a dusty black.  Further west, healthy bamboo continues, and

you can make out a winding green-grey river in the distance.

"
E
"south"
"Bamboo continues for a ways to the south, but anything else in that direction

is hidden by a thick light grey mist.

"
