"
E
"door-shaped gap bamboo 1 south"
"The arching doorway to the south must have once held an impressively thick

door, as the wall is over three feet thick and the door was meant as the main

entrance.  The masonry where the hinges once were is broken and crumbling, and

not with age alone; it appears that the door was forcibly ripped out.  Bamboo

grows right up against the empty door now, the stalks no more than three

inches apart.  Exit by this route is no longer possible.

"
