#39853
"Giant Bamboo - Marshy Ground"
"Marshy and soft, the ground of this large clearing in the bamboo squelches

with any movement.  Small tufts of swamp grass are the only plant life that

hangs on in the unstable mud.  Half-submerged bones of creatures ranging from

what look like deer, to what might be giant bears of some kind stick up at odd

angles.  Thick, thorny swamp briar has invaded the bamboo to the north and

east; the maze of giant stalks and rough undergrowth looks impassable.

Movement to the south and west is blocked by thick green walls of giant bamboo.

"
